---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Mingxi Yan">
  <Navigation />

  <main class="flex-grow">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-50 to-white">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-6 opacity-0 animate-fade-in-up">About Me</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-3xl opacity-0 animate-fade-in-up delay-100">
          A journey through code, cards, and creativity.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <section class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <!-- Introduction -->
          <div class="mb-16">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 flex items-center">
              <span class="w-12 h-1 bg-black mr-4"></span>
              Who I Am
            </h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                I'm a Computer Science student who believes that the best solutions come from the intersection of logic and creativity.
                Whether I'm debugging code, analyzing poker hands, or crafting a poem, I'm driven by the same fundamental question:
                <em>How can I understand this system well enough to master it?</em>
              </p>
              <p>
                My journey into technology started with curiosity about how things work. That curiosity evolved into a passion for
                building things that solve real problems. Along the way, I discovered that the skills that make you good at
                programming—pattern recognition, logical thinking, probabilistic reasoning—are the same skills that make you good
                at poker, philosophy, and strategic thinking in general.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Four Pillars -->
          <div class="mb-16">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 flex items-center">
              <span class="w-12 h-1 bg-black mr-4"></span>
              My Four Pillars
            </h2>

            <div class="space-y-8">
              <!-- Computer Science -->
              <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-black p-6">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">💻 Computer Science</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                  Technology is my primary lens for understanding and changing the world. I love the precise nature of code—how
                  it either works or it doesn't, how elegant solutions emerge from careful thinking. But I'm equally fascinated
                  by the human side: how do we design systems that people actually want to use? How do we make complex technology
                  accessible and intuitive?
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- Poker -->
              <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-black p-6">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">♠ Poker</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                  Poker taught me more about decision-making under uncertainty than any textbook could. Every hand is a lesson in
                  probability, psychology, and risk management. The game mirrors life: you can't control the cards you're dealt,
                  but you can control how you play them. It's a beautiful blend of mathematics and human behavior, and it's made
                  me a better thinker in every domain.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- Writing -->
              <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-black p-6">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">✍️ Writing</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                  Writing is how I make sense of the world. Whether it's poetry, essays, or philosophical musings, writing forces
                  me to clarify my thoughts and express complex ideas in simple terms. It's the counterbalance to the technical
                  precision of programming—a space where ambiguity and emotion are not bugs but features. Writing keeps me human
                  in a world of machines.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- Basketball -->
              <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-black p-6">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">🏀 Basketball</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                  Basketball is my meditation in motion. Every shot requires focus, every play demands split-second decisions,
                  and every game teaches resilience. The court is where I learned that consistency beats talent, that practice
                  makes permanent, and that the best plays come from reading the game—pattern recognition, just like debugging
                  code or reading poker tells. Whether I'm sinking a three-pointer or working through a tough algorithm, the
                  discipline is the same: repetition, refinement, results.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Philosophy -->
          <div class="mb-16">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 flex items-center">
              <span class="w-12 h-1 bg-black mr-4"></span>
              My Philosophy
            </h2>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 p-8">
              <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                <p class="text-lg italic font-serif">
                  "Be curious. Stay humble. Build things that matter."
                </p>
                <p>
                  I believe in continuous learning—not because I have to, but because I genuinely can't imagine living any other way.
                  Every skill I develop, every book I read, every conversation I have adds another tool to my mental toolkit.
                </p>
                <p>
                  I believe in systems thinking. Most problems aren't isolated; they're part of larger patterns. Whether debugging
                  code or analyzing a poker hand, the solution often lies in understanding the broader context.
                </p>
                <p>
                  I believe in balancing logic with intuition, analysis with creativity, individual excellence with collaboration.
                  The best solutions rarely come from extremes—they come from finding the right synthesis.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- What I'm Looking For -->
          <div class="mb-16">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 flex items-center">
              <span class="w-12 h-1 bg-black mr-4"></span>
              What I'm Looking For
            </h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                I'm looking for opportunities where I can apply my technical skills to meaningful problems. I want to work with
                teams that value both rigorous engineering and creative problem-solving. I'm drawn to projects at the intersection
                of technology and human experience—tools that genuinely make people's lives better.
              </p>
              <p>
                I'm also looking for conversations. If you're interested in technology, game theory, philosophy, or the intersection
                of any of these fields, I'd love to connect. Some of my best ideas have come from unexpected conversations with
                curious people.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Fun Facts -->
          <div class="mb-16">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 flex items-center">
              <span class="w-12 h-1 bg-black mr-4"></span>
              A Few More Things
            </h2>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-600">
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <span class="mr-3 text-xl">•</span>
                <span>I think the best code is code that explains itself</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <span class="mr-3 text-xl">•</span>
                <span>I believe coffee is a food group</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <span class="mr-3 text-xl">•</span>
                <span>I'm convinced that most complex problems can be solved with a whiteboard and enough time</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <span class="mr-3 text-xl">•</span>
                <span>I think the Socratic method is underrated in software development</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <span class="mr-3 text-xl">•</span>
                <span>I believe everyone should learn to play poker—it's a masterclass in decision theory</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <span class="mr-3 text-xl">•</span>
                <span>I'm always working on too many side projects simultaneously</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact Section -->
    <section class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-black text-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 text-center">Let's Talk</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 text-center">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold mb-3">Professional</h3>
            <a href="https://linkedin.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors">
              LinkedIn
            </a>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold mb-3">Code</h3>
            <a href="https://github.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors">
              GitHub
            </a>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold mb-3">Direct</h3>
            <a href="mailto:your.email@example.com" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors">
              Email
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-12 text-center">
          <p class="text-gray-400">
            Whether you want to discuss a project, share ideas, or just say hi—I'm always happy to connect.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    color: #000;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .prose h3 {
    color: #000;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
